<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at the 10.32 nm Chlamydomonas eyespot pigment stripe (Pass 2) — Morphological realism / specimen match: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Side by side, the modulated frame keeps the SEM's cells, flagella, and footer. CV similarity is 96.0 (orientation 0.965, radial FFT 1.000, coherency 0.914) on 12 frames at 1024 px. The 10 nm spot lattice is a separate panel because the micrograph cannot resolve it. That is why this is 80 rather than a near-copy score." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at the 10.32 nm Chlamydomonas eyespot pigment stripe (Pass 2) (Chlamydomonas reinhardtii (Holocene, 0 Ma))",
        "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at the 10.32 nm Chlamydomonas eyespot pigment stripe (Pass 2) faithfully reproduces Chlamydomonas reinhardtii (Holocene, 0 Ma) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Chlamydomonas reinhardtii (Holocene, 0 Ma) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Chlamydomonas reinhardtii (Holocene, 0 Ma)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim EYE2/EYE3 are dispensable.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim a published electron-micrograph measurement of exactly 10.32 nm.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the 4.72 um bright-cap equals the 10 um nominal vegetative length.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the SEM resolves that stripe. Orientation and radial spectra match because the frame keeps the real cell outlines.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Dv sweep, Dv=Du negative control (sigma_max=-0.089), and ablation of u^2 v (sigma_max=-1.00).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Segmentation of the SEM and modulation of those cell bodies by the activator field.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: k_c and k_max, with the unit chosen so lambda(k_max)=10.32 nm = 1.032e-8 m at age 0 Ma.",
        "reported_in_source: Dieckmann 2003: carotenoid granules form the eyespot under the plasma membrane.",
        "reported_in_source: Foster and Smyth 1980: quarter-wave spacing d = lambda_light / (4 n), about 93 nm for 540 nm light at n=1.45, the successor scale.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979: the activator-inhibitor rate laws used here.",
        "reported_in_source: The Dartmouth SEM labels a 10 um scale bar. This pass measures 4.72 um bright-caps on three isolated cells.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: instability at a finite critical wavenumber k_c.",
        "transfer_boundary: At 10 nm the continuum limit is a modeling choice. Diffusion constants are scaled so the selected wavelength matches the assigned detail scale; they are not measured cytoplasmic diffusivities.",
        "transfer_boundary: No fossil Chlamydomonas chronospecies is in this 1/1 series. The comparison is monomer 3.2 nm versus this stripe versus the quarter-wave spacing." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Chlamydomonas reinhardtii" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "IV. Protista & Monera" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mineralized Protists (Silica/Calcite)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Chlamydomonas" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/chlamydomonas_reinhardtii_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Chlamydomonas reinhardtii (Holocene, 0 Ma); environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: instability at a finite critical wavenumber k_c. | Schnakenberg 1979: the activator-inhibitor rate laws used here. | Foster and Smyth 1980: quarter-wave spacing d = lambda_light / (4 n), about 93 nm for 540 nm light at n=1.45, the successor scale. | Dieckmann 2003: carotenoid granules form the eyespot under the plasma membrane. | The Dartmouth SEM labels a 10 um scale bar. This pass measures 4.72 um bright-caps on three isolated cells.; reconstructed_in_script: k_c and k_max, with the unit chosen so lambda(k_max)=10.32 nm = 1.032e-8 m at age 0 Ma. | Dv sweep, Dv=Du negative control (sigma_max=-0.089), and ablation of u^2 v (sigma_max=-1.00). | Segmentation of the SEM and modulation of those cell bodies by the activator field.; transfer_boundary: At 10 nm the continuum limit is a modeling choice. Diffusion constants are scaled so the selected wavelength matches the assigned detail scale; they are not measured cytoplasmic diffusivities. | No fossil Chlamydomonas chronospecies is in this 1/1 series. The comparison is monomer 3.2 nm versus this stripe versus the quarter-wave spacing.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a published electron-micrograph measurement of exactly 10.32 nm. | Does not claim the SEM resolves that stripe. Orientation and radial spectra match because the frame keeps the real cell outlines. | Does not claim EYE2/EYE3 are dispensable. | Does not claim the 4.72 um bright-cap equals the 10 um nominal vegetative length.]; phenomenon_size: 10 nm (1.032e-08 m, log10=-7.986 m, tier=1_molecular_nm); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 10 nm to 31 µm): 10 nm:chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-bioelectric-polarity, 38 nm:chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-vertex-packing, 684 nm:chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-turing-wavelength, 1.3 µm:chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-clock-wavefront, 2.1 µm:chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-morphogen-condensation, 2.7 µm:chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-flux-canalization, 3.1 µm:chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-elastic-buckling, 6.7 µm:chlamydomonas-reinhardtii-branching-tree" ;
